From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:40:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: apq8096: pin the back end format to S16_LE

apq8096_be_hw_params_fixup() fixes the back end rate and channel count
but passes the front end sample format through. PipeWire opens the
front ends with S24_LE, and the ADSP then refuses to start the SLIMbus
AFE port:

  qcom-q6afe aprsvc:service:4:4: AFE enable for port 0x4001 failed -22
  q6afe-dai ...: fail to start AFE port 3

Only S16_LE works on these SLIMbus ports, so set it in the fixup, like
sdm845.c and sm8250.c do. The ASM front ends still accept other formats.

Tested on a Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 (APQ8096, WCD9335): headphone playback
and microphone capture through PipeWire.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/apq8096.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/apq8096.c b/sound/soc/qcom/apq8096.c
index cfd6438dbc..353f2fe69f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/apq8096.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/apq8096.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include <sound/soc.h>
 #include <sound/soc-dapm.h>
 #include <sound/pcm.h>
+#include <sound/pcm_params.h>
 #include "common.h"
 
 #define SLIM_MAX_TX_PORTS 16
@@ -19,9 +20,12 @@ static int apq8096_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 					SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_RATE);
 	struct snd_interval *channels = hw_param_interval(params,
 					SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_CHANNELS);
+	struct snd_mask *fmt = hw_param_mask(params, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_FORMAT);
 
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
 	channels->min = channels->max = 2;
+	snd_mask_none(fmt);
+	snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
 
 	return 0;
 }
